    <string name="backup_help_cd">Help</string>
    <string name="backup_help_title">WebDAV backup help</string>
    <string name="backup_help_intro_title">Overview</string>
    <string name="backup_help_intro_body">This app supports cloud backup via the WebDAV protocol. Any WebDAV-compatible cloud works; Nutstore (Jianguoyun) is recommended (about 1 GB free traffic per month is usually enough). The daily backup zip has library metadata, groups, progress, bookmarks, highlights, reading settings, and profile (no bodies); missing bodies go to books/{content-hash}.zip. Books are identified across devices by content hash, not local auto-increment ids. Import/delete syncs bodies; you can also use Backup / Restore book bodies manually.</string>
    <string name="backup_help_jianguoyun_title">Nutstore setup</string>
    <string name="backup_help_jianguoyun_body">1. Open https://www.jianguoyun.com/\n2. Sign up or sign in\n3. Open Account info from the top-right menu\n4. Go to Security\n5. Under third-party apps, add an app and create an app password\n6. Enter the server URL, account, and app password in Me → Backup &amp; restore\n7. Keep the default subdirectory (MdReader) unless you need another\n8. Run a manual backup once to verify\n9. To restore, pick the backup file you want</string>
    <string name="backup_help_auto_title">Auto backup</string>
    <string name="backup_help_auto_body">• After WebDAV is configured, the app auto-backs up once a day when you exit (back-to-exit works; force-stopping from Recents may not)\n• Same-day backups with the same filename overwrite; different dates are kept\n• If “Also upload latest backup” is on, remote backup.zip is also overwritten for quick restore\n• If “Check for new backups on launch” is on, a newer cloud backup prompts for a merge restore</string>
    <string name="backup_help_tips_title">Tips</string>
    <string name="backup_help_tips_body">• First backup fails: create a MdReader folder at the WebDAV root, then retry\n• Auth fails: use the app password, not your login password\n• Switching devices: on the source, Backup then Backup book bodies; on the new device, Restore then Restore book bodies\n• The same book imported on multiple devices merges by content hash and will not overwrite via colliding local ids\n• Metadata restore merges updates and keeps device-only books\n• After restore, restart the app so all settings apply\n• WebDAV credentials stay on this device and are not overwritten by a restore package</string>
